Package: osirad
Title: PET Voxels and Radiomics from 'OsiriX' Regions of Interest
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Tao", "Lan", email = "lantao32405@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Eric", "Wolsztynski", email = "eric.w@ucc.ie", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Reads regions of interest (ROIs) drawn in the 'OsiriX' medical
    image viewer and exported as XML files, and recovers the exact voxels of
    each ROI on the positron emission tomography (PET) series stored as
    Digital Imaging and Communications in Medicine (DICOM) files. The voxels
    are found by matching the voxel values stored in the XML file to the
    standardised uptake values (SUV) computed from the DICOM header. The
    resulting voxel table (positions in pixels and millimetres, and SUV) can be
    passed to the 'Python' library 'PyRadiomics' (van Griethuysen et al. (2017)
    <doi:10.1158/0008-5472.CAN-17-0339>) through 'reticulate' to compute
    radiomics features.
